From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:33:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini-station: latch microSD read data
 one clock later

At SDR104 the microSD slot fails about 2 % of multi-block reads with a
data CRC error. The failures follow bus idle time, and the 64-cell tuning
passes throughout. The tuning settles on 45-47 pad delay cells with the
default data latch clock.

The vendor kernel reads the same card cleanly, with the same reads and
the same request size. It latches read data one internal clock later
and needs only 8 delay cells. With that latch and delay written at
runtime, 942 reads ran without an error, against 23 of 1045 with the
mainline values on the same boot.

Set mediatek,latch-ck to 1 so that the tuning works from the later
latch.

The runtime test also set the CKGEN delay to 0, which mtk-sd fixes at 1;
this change leaves it at 1. Not yet run on hardware.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
index da19e3c..ebb7c3b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
@@ -750,6 +750,13 @@
 	cd-supply = <&mt6351_vmch_reg>;
 	vmmc-supply = <&mt6351_vmch_reg>;
 	vqmmc-supply = <&mt6351_vmc_reg>;
+	/*
+	 * Latch read data one internal clock later, as the vendor kernel
+	 * does. With latch 0 the tuning settles on about 47 delay cells,
+	 * and reads that start after the bus has been idle fail CRC a few
+	 * percent of the time although the tuning block passes.
+	 */
+	mediatek,latch-ck = <1>;
 	no-mmc;
 	no-sdio;
 	status = "okay";
